---
// The single "payment settled" state, used wherever a demo conversation reaches
// checkout (hero mini-chat and the full conversation). Keeping it in one
// component means the paid state can only ever look one way.
//
// A tick, not a dot: the badge marks a settled outcome, so a static
// confirmation mark is truer to the state than a "live" indicator. The generic
// `.status` pill stays tick-free because it also carries neutral states
// ("ready") and negative ones ("Incomplete"), where a tick would lie.
//
// The tick ink is centred in its own viewBox (y 3.5 to 8.5 of 12) and the label
// runs at line-height 1, so the two boxes and the ink inside them line up and
// plain `align-items: center` centres the type itself in every engine.
---

<span class="paid-badge">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M2.5 6 5 8.5l4.5-5" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
  </svg>
  <span>Paid · order confirmed</span>
</span>
